index 0000000..de1d90c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/functions/json.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+### JSON access operators
+
+| Operator | Arguments      | Return | Description                                                                 |
+| -------- | -------------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| ->       | (Text, Any)    | Text   | Select a member/element and return it as JSON text.                         |
+| ->>      | (Text, Any)    | Any    | Select a member/element and return it as a typed value (containers as text).|
+
+The right operand selects an object member when it is text, the array element `[n]`
+when it is an integer, or a JSON path when it begins with `$`. `->` returns JSON text,
+while `->>` returns a typed value (a JSON null becomes SQL null) that composes in
+arithmetic and comparisons, e.g. `(document ->> 'age') + 1`. The operators are
+left-associative and bind tighter than arithmetic, so `document ->> 'n' + 1` groups as
+`(document ->> 'n') + 1`.
+
+### JSON path syntax
+
+| Form           | Description                                     |
+| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
+| `$`            | The document root.                              |
+| `.key`         | An object member; `."quoted key"` when needed.  |
+| `[n]`          | The array element at zero-based index `n`.      |
+| `[#]`          | The position past the last element (append).    |
+| `[#-n]`        | The element `n` places from the end.            |
+
+A malformed path or a lookup with no value yields null. `json_query` additionally
+accepts `.*` (each member value or array element), `[*]` (each array element),
+`..key`/`.."key"` (each such member at any depth) and `..*` (each value); it rejects
+the `[#]` forms.
+
+### JSON functions
+
+| Name              | Parameters               | Return  | Description                                                                        |
+| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| JSON              | Text                     | Text    | Reparse a document and return minified JSON.                                       |
+| JSON_VALID        | Text                     | Boolean | Report whether the argument is valid JSON.                                         |
+| JSON_TYPE         | Text, Text?              | Text    | The type tag of the value at an optional path.                                     |
+| JSON_EXTRACT      | Text, Text, ...Text      | Any     | The value at one path (typed), or a JSON array for several paths.                  |
+| JSON_QUERY        | Text, Text               | Text    | A JSON array of every match of an extended path, in document pre-order.            |
+| JSON_ARRAY        | ...Any                   | Text    | Build a JSON array from the arguments.                                             |
+| JSON_OBJECT       | ...Any                   | Text    | Build a JSON object from alternating key/value arguments.                          |
+| JSON_ARRAY_LENGTH | Text, Text?              | Integer | The array length at an optional path, zero for a non-array.                        |
+| JSON_QUOTE        | Any                      | Text    | Render a value as JSON.                                                            |
+| JSON_SET          | Text, Text, Any, ...     | Text    | Write each path whether or not it exists.                                          |
+| JSON_INSERT       | Text, Text, Any, ...     | Text    | Write each path only when it is absent.                                            |
+| JSON_REPLACE      | Text, Text, Any, ...     | Text    | Write each path only when it is present.                                           |
+| JSON_REMOVE       | Text, Text, ...Text      | Text    | Delete the values at the paths left to right, reindexing arrays.                   |
+| JSON_PATCH        | Text, Text               | Text    | Apply an RFC 7396 merge patch (null members remove; a non-object patch replaces).  |
+| JSON_KEYS         | Text                     | Text    | An object's member names as a JSON array, or null for a non-object.                |
+| JSON_CONTAINS     | Text, Text               | Boolean | Whether a candidate is recursively contained in the target.                        |
+| JSON_DEPTH        | Text                     | Integer | The nesting depth, one for scalars and empty containers.                           |
+| JSON_PRETTY       | Text                     | Text    | Re-serialise the document with indentation.                                        |
+
+### Mutation semantics
+
+`JSON_SET`, `JSON_INSERT` and `JSON_REPLACE` apply alternating path/value pairs left to
+right, and an updated member keeps its position. For set and replace a `$` path replaces
+the whole document, while insert leaves it unchanged. A mutation whose parent is absent
+leaves the document unchanged, and only `[#]` appends: an out-of-range `[n]` or a `[#-n]`
+before the front is not an append and leaves the array untouched. Functions consuming a
+JSON document return null when it is invalid, and output is minified except for
+`JSON_PRETTY`.
